{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384853-wu-lung","id":1384853,"title":"Wu Lung","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T09:14:34-07:00","id":1384853,"title":"Wu Lung","content":"My game is currently taking place in Shanghai during the Solitary Island period (1938 CE). My mages are maneuvering between a rogue Tremere elder who escaped the Brujah purge in Russia and the last Wu Lung Master in the city.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure which way the story will go, so I'm prepping the NPCs as if they will be attacked. The Tremere is already dealt with so now I'm focusing on the Wu Lung Master. He is of the Dragon School, so Spirit is his primary. Taking their reliance on dogma and procedure, I figure he'll have plenty of prepared and ongoing spells, hence my question:<br /> <br /> Which war-time defenses would you give a Wu Lung Dragon Master in a besieged paradigm?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:58:59-07:00","id":1384863,"title":"","content":"Stone guardians foo dogs, dragons, animated weapons. He could have bound spirts into all sorts of crazy stuff to let your mind go wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":